# Package boundaries

Canonical guidance: [`.github/contributing.md`](../../.github/contributing.md) (project structure / importing packages), package `package.json` / `src/index.ts`, [`scripts/aliases.js`](../../scripts/aliases.js), [`rollup.config.js`](../../rollup.config.js). Prefer current adjacent patterns in the same package.

## Required

- Identify whether behavior is compiler/runtime, platform-agnostic/platform-specific, public/internal, and source/generated before selecting a file.
- Use package-name imports for cross-package dependencies (`@vue/runtime-core`), never relative paths across package roots.
- Declare dependencies when adding non-type imports or re-exported types.
- Keep compiler and runtime dependency graphs separate.
- Prefer existing package abstractions and current nearby patterns.
- For hot-path/runtime work, call out allocation, branching, code size, and dev/prod impact.
- Put development-only logic under `__DEV__` where consistent with current code.

## Prohibited

- No relative imports that cross package roots.
- No compiler → runtime or runtime → compiler imports (do not expand existing type-only exceptions casually).
- No casual extraction to `@vue/shared`; shared code must be environment-neutral and justify bundle reach.
- No compiler-only `@vue/shared` helpers (e.g. `isHTMLTag`, `isSVGTag`) in runtime paths.
- No package dependency change without checking build formats and published consumption.
